# Checkout needs a signed-in user AND the cart_token cookie. GoLand's HTTP client
# keeps both the cookie and {{accessToken}} between requests, so run these in order.
#
# Paying in the browser (Stripe test mode):
#   1. Run "Checkout" and open the checkoutUrl from the response.
#   2. Pay with the test card 4242 4242 4242 4242, any future expiry date
#      (e.g. 12/34), any CVC and any name.
#   3. Stripe sends you to FRONTEND_URL/orders/{orderId}?paid=1.
#
# The order only becomes paid when the webhook arrives, so for local runs start
# the Stripe CLI first (it prints a whsec_... secret; put it in .env as
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET and restart the API):
#   stripe listen --forward-to localhost:8080/api/v1/webhooks/stripe
#
# offerId is PixelVault's Elden Ring offer. Offer ids change after seed -reset;
# take a new one from the offers of GET /api/v1/products/{slug}.
@offerId = f26f9e4f-2b98-405d-9b59-c9044d33566c

### Login
# Seeded users all use the password Password123!.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "emma.johnson@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

> {% client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### Add item to cart
# Sets the cart_token cookie on the first add.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "offerId": "{{offerId}}"
}

### Checkout
# 201 {"orderId": "...", "checkoutUrl": "https://checkout.stripe.com/..."}.
# 400 cart_empty without a cart or items, 409 offer_unavailable or insufficient_stock
# if an offer can't be bought, 502 payment_provider_error if Stripe fails.
# The keys stay reserved for 35 minutes; the cart is emptied only after payment.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
